:"Special Weather Statement issued August 26 at 2:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 244 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over\nGuffey, or 36 miles west of Colorado Springs, moving southeast at 15\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nWaugh Mountain.","ends":"2026-08-26T15:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Northwestern Fremont County  Above 8500Ft; Western/Central Fremont County Below 8500 Ft; Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Canon City Vicinity/Eastern Fremont County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7eea3e2b02c5c3809f9b566c29b691c8b13e3837.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7eea3e2b02c5c3809f9b566c29b691c8b13e3837.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued August 26 at 2:35PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"At 234 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nManitou Springs, or 7 miles west of Colorado Springs, moving east at\n15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and half inch hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSouthwestern Colorado Springs, Fountain, Manitou Springs, Victor,\nStratmoor, Fort Carson, Security, and Security-Widefield.","ends":"2026-08-26T15:00:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Teller County/Rampart Range above 7500fT/Pike's Peak Between 7500 And 11000 Ft; Pikes Peak above 11000 Ft; Colorado Springs Vicinity/Southern El Paso County/Rampart Range Below 7400 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.05fd2622f20d409e4bc9566b786ea82b748793be.001.1","url":"https://api.weather